        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "No, unfortunately, there is no functionality for searching only within scope. You can use other tools for that and 'ibhagwan/fzf-lua` is a fine choice.\r\n\r\nI don't really know how to do that though. If I understand you correctly, it would be enough for you to get actual lines within current indent scope? If so, here is a function which can do that:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n_G.get_scope_lines = function()\r\n  local scope = MiniIndentscope.get_scope()\r\n  if scope.border.indent < 0 then return {} end\r\n  return vim.api.nvim_buf_get_lines(scope.buf_id, scope.border.top - 1, scope.border.bottom, true)\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt returns lines inside scope including its border. If you want to exclude borders, replace `scope.border` with `scope.body`. Note that it will differ for lines with zero indent: with border it will return to lines, without it - all buffer lines. Tweak this for your liking.\r\n\r\nDoes this answer your question?",
