            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "That does work! It returns me all the lines in the current scope as expected. Now, I just have to pass it to fzf-lua properly to get it to work. Thank you so much!\r\n\r\nI had one other question about scopes within comments. Is there a way to get scopes working for comments as well? Sometimes, I'll comment large body of code and uncommenting them would be easy. I can use relative numbers for that for sure but thought I'd ask.",
