        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I had one other question about scopes within comments. Is there a way to get scopes working for comments as well? Sometimes, I'll comment large body of code and uncommenting them would be easy. I can use relative numbers for that for sure but thought I'd ask.\r\n\r\nI amfraid, no. Indent scope is computed based on text indent, that is a maximum whitespace from line start. As start of comment is (almost surely) not a whitespace, it is used to compute indent level.\r\n\r\nI use comment textobject for this purpose: with 'mini.comment' pressing `gcgc` toggles comment (first `gc`) for a comment textobject (second `gc`). Not sure if 'Comment.nvim' has it, though.\r\n\r\nAs original question is cleared, I'll close this then.",
